# gitleaks — historical synthetic test credentials (2026-10-06, beta release)
#
# Each line is a gitleaks fingerprint, <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>, so it
# exempts ONE finding in ONE historical commit and nothing else. Any new commit
# that adds a secret — including to these same files, or the same value again —
# produces a new fingerprint and is still reported. Detection stays fully on;
# no rule, path or value pattern is disabled.
#
# Why fingerprints and not inline  (the policy in
# security-audit.yml): the inline marker exempts a line in NEW commits. These 24
# findings live in commits that are already in history, whose contents cannot
# change without rewriting history. They surfaced only in the weekly full-history
# scan (push/PR scans check just the new commit range), which has failed every
# week since at least 2026-09-14 on them.
#
# Every value below was decoded and checked by hand before being listed; all
# are synthetic: Fernet-format keys whose base64 decodes to a descriptive
# stockassist test phrase, JWT-shaped strings whose payload is the literal word
# SECRET, and self-describing test strings (chaos, nova, live-looking and
# placeholder OAuth values). Example values are deliberately NOT quoted here:
# quoting them in this file would itself trip the scanner on the commit that
# adds it. Regenerate with gitleaks v8.24.3
# (the version gitleaks-action pins) and never add a fingerprint without
# checking the value it hides.
